    "message": "test(mcp): scope the UNC staleness case to Windows\n\nA UNC path is a network location only on Windows, where stat fails on an\nunreachable one with something other than ENOENT — which is the whole point of\nthe assertion. Everywhere else those backslashes are ordinary filename\ncharacters, the path really is absent, and `stale` is the right answer, so the\ntest failed on both Linux runners and both macOS runners while passing on\nWindows where it was written. Confirmed against Linux directly rather than by\nanother CI round-trip.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
